    {
      "who": "pending (owner)",
      "when": null,
      "gate": "piece",
      "status": "pending",
      "revision": "matte-leaves",
      "requested": "2026-10-26",
      "notes": "Pending owner review; not an approval. Rebuilt for the owner's bug report (2026-10-26, \"these bushes are too shiny\"): the leaf texels' roughness (ORM G) was 0.50-0.64, glossy on the dark round mass, so the sky's specular lay across the top of the bush as a grey sheen at low play cameras. _verge_bush.py now maps it linearly onto 0.76-0.86 (mean 0.81 over the opaque texels, the grass draws at 0.78); the shade blob (0.85) keep theirs. Only the ORM's G changed: albedo, normal and masks PNGs, the mesh, LODs, collider and sockets are byte-identical to the approved build (the albedo and normal KTX2 re-encode under the current single-threaded UASTC settings). Before and after in play: docs/checkpoints/bush-shine/sheet.jpg. The controller records the owner's decision."
    }
